  "content": "Date.parse(s.ts) can return NaN if s.ts is undefined or not a valid date string. When that happens, ageMs becomes NaN, the freshness comparison evaluates to false (NaN < X is always false), and the verdict silently degrades to \"STALE\". Additionally, NaN would be emitted in the output payload. Add a validity check on the parsed timestamp before proceeding.",
